From: AROS eza port maintainers
Date: 2026-10-21
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt eza platform boundaries for AROS ABIv11
Repository: eza
Base-Commit: 98442ab17c2c3738701b62a7e060b1431ae2d6ea
Preceding-Patches: none
Upstream-Status: local-only
Scope: x86_64 AROS ABIv11; other targets retain upstream implementations.

Use Output() presentation capabilities and native DOS protection instead of
unsupported Unix terminal/account interfaces. Keep redirection plain, map ANSI
palette colours to indexed SGR, preserve AmigaDOS names and invalid bytes, and
run directory formatting sequentially so global worker lifetime cannot prevent
return to the Shell. Disable unsupported icons and hyperlinks explicitly.

Verification: eight host policy tests pass; target links with the pinned
rust-aros baseline. Initial native run passed help/version but exposed a
worker-lifetime hang and volume-prefixed names. The sequential/name fixes
require native rerun; this patch is not yet release-validated.
Removal: replace individual adaptations when upstream supports the same AROS
contracts and passes native regression coverage. No upstream submission made.

